cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  SentiLight — Policy-Space Reformulation for Affective
  Smart-Lighting Control (research artifacts)
message: >-
  If you use these artifacts, please cite this record and the
  associated paper.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Baik
    given-names: Seongbok
repository-code: 'https://github.com/sbbaik/SentiLight'
abstract: >-
  Code, evaluation data, per-row predictions and preregistrations
  for a study of output formulation versus model scale in
  affective smart-lighting control. The control task is governed
  by a finite policy of 240 reachable (H, S, B, Dimmer, CT)
  actions; reformulating generation as classification over that
  action space lets a 23M model exceed a 60M generative model on
  policy compliance. A 2x2 decomposition attributes most of the
  gain to aligning training data with the policy rather than to
  the output head, and a constrained-decoding control shows that
  projecting generative outputs onto the valid action set after
  the fact recovers none of the gap.
keywords:
  - structured output
  - constrained decoding
  - compact language models
  - on-device inference
  - affective computing
  - smart lighting
  - preregistration
  - reproducibility
license: Apache-2.0
